# KSI-CNA-ULN: Azure Virtual Network - Logical Network Segmentation
# Validates VNet is provisioned with subnets for traffic flow control

META
    esp_id `ksi-cna-uln-az-vnet-baseline-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `azure`
    criticality `high`

    title `KSI-CNA-ULN: Azure VNet - logical network segmentation`
    description `Validates that the virtual network is provisioned with subnets defined for network segmentation and traffic flow enforcement`
    author `security-team`
    tags `azure,vnet,network,segmentation,subnets`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-CNA-ULN,KSI:KSI-CNA-RNT,NIST:SC-7,NIST:AC-4`
    control_objective `KSI-CNA-ULN`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `cloud-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `7`
    recommendation `Ensure all workloads are deployed into virtual networks with appropriate subnet segmentation and NSGs attached to each subnet`

    impl_KSI_CNA_ULN `Logical networking is validated by confirming the virtual network exists (found=true) and is successfully provisioned (provisioningState=Succeeded) with at least one subnet defined (subnet_count>=1). Virtual networks provide the foundational network isolation boundary in Azure, and subnet segmentation within VNets enables microsegmentation of workloads and enforcement of traffic flow controls via NSGs and route tables.`

    impl_KSI_CNA_RNT `Network traffic restriction is supported by the virtual network providing the isolation boundary within which NSGs can be applied to subnets and NICs to filter inbound and outbound traffic.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT vnet_demo
        name `vnet-example-prod`
        resource_group `rg-example-eastus`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE st_vnet_segmented
        found boolean = true
        provisioning_state string = `Succeeded`
        subnet_count int >= 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN az_virtual_network
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF st_vnet_segmented
            OBJECT_REF vnet_demo
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
